      "text": "Stick, to set up an automated “capture → compare → repair” loop we need four concrete pieces:\n\n1. **Baseline definition** – where does the “before” state live? (e.g., Git commit, DB snapshot, config file, IaC manifest) and how is it refreshed.\n2. **Current state source** – what you’ll poll for the “after” snapshot (API endpoint, command output, DB query, etc.).\n3. **Drift detection logic** – hash/checksum, diff, rule‑engine, or schema validation you prefer.\n4. **Repair mechanism** – rollback to baseline, idempotent apply‑only script, or orchestrated sync (Ansible, Terraform, custom CLI).\n\nOnce I have those details I can draft a concrete workflow (or ready‑to‑run scripts) that continuously reconciles the two states and self‑heals any deviation. What system are we targeting, and what existing artefacts (snapshots, manifests, tools) are already in place?",
